Removed two unreachable branches from :meth:`~icalendar.prop.org.vOrg.from_ical` and :meth:`~icalendar.prop.org.vOrg.from_jcal`: the ``len(fields) < 1`` check in ``from_ical`` could never be true because :func:`~icalendar.parser.split_on_unescaped_semicolon` always returns at least one element, and the ``len(jcal_property) < 4`` check in ``from_jcal`` was redundant with the validation already performed by :meth:`~icalendar.error.JCalParsingError.validate_property`. No behavior change for callers. I used Claude Code (Anthropic's Claude Sonnet 5) to identify and remove the dead branches and to update the accompanying coverage tests; I reviewed the diff and ran the test suite locally. @vjymisal0
